{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>״אֲשֶׁר אֶשְׁמַע וְגוֹ׳ לְשַׁלַּח״ וְגוֹ׳.</b> He intends to say: what is His great power — that I should hearken to His voice in so great a matter as to send [Israel], and so forth? And he returned to say that his words were stated for emphasis — even if He should be very great, that would not avail to send Israel. And his intention in this is not that he knows Him but considers Him insufficiently great to send Israel; rather, he does not know Him at all, and that is what he said: <b>״לֹא יָדַעְתִּי״</b> וְגוֹ׳. And his saying <b>״וְגַם״</b> — meaning: and even if He makes it known to him and impresses upon him that He is great, nevertheless, ״אֶת יִשְׂרָאֵל לֹא״ וְגוֹ׳ — and these are the beginning of his words. Understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:42.877243161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}